# Allow-list, not a deny-list. The build needs Go sources and nothing else, and
# anything new in the repo is junk to it by default — a kubeconfig written by a
# test run has already landed here once, and COPY . . would have put cluster
# credentials in a build layer.
#
# Safe in the direction a deny-list is not: if the build ever does need a file,
# it fails at compile time rather than silently shipping without it.
*

!**/*.go
!go.mod
!go.sum

# Embedded by gateway/crds.go. Without this go:embed fails the build, which is
# the loud failure an allow-list is chosen for.
!gateway/crds/zz_generated.*.yaml
